# Data files — inventory lives in Supabase, NOT git
# 2026-11-01 hardening: the public/downloads CSV allowlist was REMOVED — the
# owner exports carry raw owner mobiles (PII) and were publicly downloadable
# from sierra-estates.net. They are quarantined to ./quarantine/ (ignored)
# and the Master Sheet now ingests via the two-way API sync (workflow 14)
# instead of IMPORTDATA over public CSV URLs.
data/
*.xlsx
*.csv
Inventory_with_Photos_Airtable.csv
inventory_*.csv
memory_*.csv
Sierra_Estates_*.csv
owner_media_matches.json
obsidian-store.json
!apps/sierra-estates-realty/data/online-sheet-units.json
!apps/sierra-estates-realty/data/consolidated-master-inventory.json
# NOTE: snapshot.json is deliberately COMMITTED — four routes statically import
# it (inventory, listings, inventory/download, admin whatsapp scan) and the
# public map serves it as the offline fallback, so a clean checkout must
# contain it. scripts/generate-inventory-snapshot.mjs refreshes it at build.
# Build artifact: prebuild mirrors repo supabase/migrations into the app for
# the runtime applier lambda. NOTE: when Vercel builds with
# rootDirectory=apps/sierra-estates-realty the repo root is unreachable, so
# the TRACKED mirror files are the only migration source there — new mirror
# migrations MUST be force-added (git add -f apps/sierra-estates-realty/
# supabase/migrations/<file>). __tests__/supabase-migration-mirror.test.ts
# fails if a mirror file is on disk but not committed.
apps/sierra-estates-realty/supabase/
apps/sierra-estates-realty/data/master-inventory-9k.json

